    package P; sub cls { "Q" } package Q; sub new { bless {v => $_[1]}, $_[0] } package main;
    my $o = bless {}, "P"; my $m = "cls";
    my $s = $o->$m(1)->new(7); print ref($s), " ", $s->{v}, "\n";

perl: Q 7.   PCL: `PCL: statement dropped at ... line 3: my $s = $o->$m(1)->new(7); -- Bug. Fell through. Missing case: [bless( {id => 7, type => methodcall}, PPIreference ), bless( {id => 0, type => methodcall}, PPIreference )]` and the run dies at the site.

The postfix `->` after a DYNAMIC-name method call is not handled where the static-name chain `$o->cls(1)->new(7)` is (probe that control).  Layer: Pl/PExpr.pm's postfix method-call chain (the methodcall node whose method is a variable).  Unblocks PPI under PCL (docs/eval-in-cl-plan.md P1): with the line split by hand PPI's output equals perl's on Calc.pm.  Probe also: `$o->$m->new`, `$o->$m()->[0]`, `$o->$m(1)->{k}`, `Class->$m(1)->new`, `$o->$cref(1)->new` (a code ref in the variable).

=== DONE (s536g) ===
Mechanism: the term fold (`Pl::PExpr::_fold_terms`, #153's walker) started a term at the `( args )` after `-> $m` -- by then a raw List / `<tree_val>`, not a `<funcall>` as a static `name(args)` is (the chain walker's W1) -- so `(1)->new(7)` folded into its own methodcall and `$o->$m` was left beside it with no arguments: "Missing case: [methodcall, methodcall]", the statement DROPPED.  Fix (the static form's continuation, rule 11): the fold never starts a term at the `( args )` of `-> NAME` / `-> ${EXPR}`, and `_term_extent` takes a `<tree_val>` argument list like a raw one, so the embedded spellings (`f($o->$m(1)->new(7)->{v}, 2)`, `($o->$m(1)->new(3)->x, 4)`) bound too.  perl = tree: `$o->$m(1)->new(7)`, `$o->$m->x`, `$o->$m(1)->[0]`, `->{k}`, `$o->$cref(1)->new`, `$o->${\ "cls"}(1)->new(7)`, `Class->$m(1)->new`, `$o->$m (1)` with a space, `$o->$n(2) + 3`, `($o->$m, (1))`.  Guard Pl/t/deref-arrow-01.t row 7 (fails on ba7863a3).  Commit a3bf120b.


